menu "Muse voice (ESP-Mosaico)"

    config MOSAICO_TTS_URL
        string "Speech server URL"
        default ""
        help
            An OpenAI-style /v1/audio/speech endpoint on the LAN that streams
            16-bit mono PCM (response_format "pcm", rate in the
            x-audio-sample-rate header), such as a computer's Qwen3-TTS
            service: http://<address>:<port>/v1/audio/speech. The board asks
            for "sample_rate": 16000 and "pace": 1.5 (a second ahead, then
            1.5 times speech), which a server may ignore at the cost of
            Wi-Fi memory. It says every
            reply, Chinese or English; when it can't be reached, Chinese is
            said by esp-sr on the board. Empty: esp-sr only. It names a
            machine on one network, so set it in sdkconfig.local.

    config MOSAICO_TTS_VOICE
        string "Speech server voice"
        default "vivian"
        help
            The server's voice name, as its /health lists them.

    config MOSAICO_TTS_BENCH
        bool "Bench RPCs over ESP-Iris (debugging)"
        default n
        help
            ESP-Iris RPC service 29524 (tts_bench.c): 1 fetches speech from
            the server (and plays it), 2 hammers PSRAM data from both cores,
            3 reads both cores' PMP registers. Used to reproduce and pin down
            the PSRAM crashes of 2026-10-04/05.

endmenu
